# What this repository is for
#
# The notes are the truth. Everything derived from them is rebuildable from a
# clean checkout, so none of it belongs in history: a 13 MB SQLite file that is
# rewritten by every `librarian index` run would add a new copy to every commit
# and would be the largest thing here within a week.
#
# The rule this file encodes is the one `.Data/README.md` already states:
# `Databases/` is disposable, `surveys/` is evidence.


# --- Derived stores: delete them, rebuild them -------------------------------
#
#   python -m librarian index               catalogue_index.sqlite
#   python -m librarian components build    source_components.sqlite
#
# `.Data/surveys/` is deliberately NOT ignored. Each file is what a blobless
# shallow clone returned on a known date and is what the structural claims in
# the notes are checked against; it cannot be regenerated without the network
# and the GitHub budget, and regenerating it against today's HEAD would destroy
# the thing that makes it evidence.
.Data/Databases/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db-journal

# Embedding vectors ride in the index above; if that ever changes, they are
# still derived and still belong here.
.Data/embeddings/


# --- The airlock ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Staged proposals are in-flight work, not evidence: a proposal is either
# promoted, at which point the note is the record, or abandoned. `.Data/briefs/`
# is deliberately NOT ignored - a brief holds why a candidate was rejected, and
# that is the negative result nothing else in the vault records.
.Data/staging/


# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/


# --- Obsidian ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The vault's shared configuration is tracked - core plugins, appearance and
# graph settings describe the vault and should travel with it. Window layout
# does not: `workspace.json` records which panes this machine had open and
# changes on every focus change.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json


# --- Working state -----------------------------------------------------------
# Mode D clones and anything the workbench opens are temporary by construction.
.Data/workbench/
.Data/clones/
scratch/
*.tmp


# --- Credentials --------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here today. Present so a GITHUB_TOKEN cannot arrive by accident.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.token


# --- OS ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
